# Copy to .env and add the same non-secret configuration names used by CABB.
ALMA_API_KEY=your_api_key_here

# Valid values: America, Europe, Asia Pacific, Canada, China
ALMA_API_REGION=America

# Web mode requires BOTH existing absolute storage directories.
# dg-landing currently uses $HOME/gems-pilot; /data is not ready.
# Create pilot roots first; the host cannot access campus //storage.
# Examples use sysadmin; use the actual Linux home path from `echo "$HOME"`.
# Shell variables are not expanded here, including $YOUR_LINUX_USER.
# Use absolute paths here, not literal $HOME or ~.
# Desktop mode retains ~/.GEMS-data unless these are configured.
# GEMS_CONFIG_DIR=/home/sysadmin/gems-pilot/config
# GEMS_DATA_DIR=/home/sysadmin/gems-pilot/data

# Alternatively select a private external environment file with
# --env-file "$HOME/gems-pilot/config/gems.env" on the Linux command line,
# or GEMS_ENV_FILE. See INSTALL-LINUX.md for the later migration to /data.
# Never commit real secrets. Encryption at rest must be provided by the
# approved storage/secret-management system, not a key saved beside this file.